    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Introduced in MongoDB 8.0, $querySettings returns settings previously added with setQuerySettings; stored settings apply cluster-wide and survive restarts. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/querySettings.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ec69e062710fd909146db1ab8c98724a8aa4b9959fbc635164e452068655f760",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:db93abda148d24de9562b842190a692db97458e90d8367aaf5407e1009f2e422"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/setquerysettings/",
            "https://docs.percona.com/percona-clustersync-for-mongodb/pqs.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "An allowedIndexes entry in inspected settings does not prove the winning plan used an index: MongoDB documents that the planner may still choose a collection scan. Check the actual explain plan. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/setquerysettings/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c12d1d07221dbebaeabcaa0f5355e4e5304c66045b28f528ba6617700f37f3d1",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2587bacb8c8c7ced8c4d23e8bbf3745a6a5b3f5df2c1ca53639f992cb6c99d20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For hash-created settings, representativeQuery is initially absent. Starting with MongoDB 8.3 and FCV 8.3 or later, a matching query schedules asynchronous, best-effort backfill; the first matching execution need not complete it. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/setquerysettings/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ae7d864b3c0ece8e3b9fa06f61c523fca39ee81c939d32c74dca96c13cc61ffc",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1301cb6c18fe245d4dace11d599d1d85ae69a4217f803f9147c145af6345d862"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "NoSQLBooster 11.2 documents the fluent inspection helper db.aggregate().querySettings({ showDebugQueryShape: true }). This is client-specific syntax; the server stage remains $querySettings. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-26)",
          "source": "https://www.nosqlbooster.com/blog/announcing-nosqlbooster-11-2/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:82368dbf5eae63ecbb9b783402ed3ebaa09f70d7cfa027a9b6a0ea2d3fe4cb9e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3392a5ba798b010d51f767f932c7310543de85964bb2876dfb1751e71b2b9829",
            "ev:ad280167e23a7981d4b8e2c48a1bfc20c84d82cde8dbdb5ebfcaf54a47ddc64a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/querySettings.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For resumable-index-build research, treat $querySettings as query-planning configuration context: the documented output describes stored query shapes and settings, not index-build progress or resume state. This scope conclusion is an inference from the documented interface. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/querySettings.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b2220bc7cc11dbda29243cb1744fb6d8c02c09d08e1b7b2ba4167b4f18c6badd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:08eba64c5fc76c68dc7d21a241f4f6f8524f242cffcf9ee9105e27eff4039efd",
            "ev:db93abda148d24de9562b842190a692db97458e90d8367aaf5407e1009f2e422"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not assume every settings entry has representativeQuery. Settings created using a query-shape hash initially omit it, and Percona explicitly handles exported entries without that field. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/setquerysettings/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:76bebd70b678b0c00531de4eefe704afdecdb9550d1e80c58f0ab55e10410ba5",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1301cb6c18fe245d4dace11d599d1d85ae69a4217f803f9147c145af6345d862",
            "ev:7e015563af7c0fd9c5cb5794128e3b31746aa935b508ae877dc175d4d24a0ac1"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://docs.percona.com/percona-clustersync-for-mongodb/pqs.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The MongoDB stage reference lists Atlas, Enterprise, and Community compatibility, but explicitly excludes Atlas M0 and Flex clusters. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/querySettings.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:2c721f32c73e21901a9eccbdce0a4462502b3f33533bc3076171eed368fee25e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:b49ec0fd39382a2de7aeec7baf668bb55f63845f73079a591003b6c20c2583fe"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/setquerysettings/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Percona ClusterSync documentation says persistent query settings require manual migration after replication is finalized; its procedure exports them with $querySettings and reapplies them with setQuerySettings. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-13)",
          "source": "https://docs.percona.com/percona-clustersync-for-mongodb/pqs.html",
